<%# What the Kiosk engine stores at this origin. Each item it shows follows from this origin's configuration. %>
<h2>What Kiosk stores for an AI assistant</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>The assistant's key.</strong> An AI assistant that registers gives us its public key. We store it with
    the account it acts for, the label you give it, its spending cap and when it was linked. We never receive its
    private key. An assistant that registers on its own gets an account with no e-mail address.</li>
  <li><strong>Link codes.</strong> When you link an assistant to your account, we store a hash of the code, never the
    code. A code expires 15 minutes after we make it.</li>
  <li><strong>Call counts.</strong> We count the calls of each assistant account since its last proof of work, and we
    record the value of each visit you complete. The call toll reads both.</li>
  <li><strong>Events.</strong> We keep each event that we send to your assistant, for example a confirmation, for
    24 hours. Then we delete it.</li>
  <% if Kiosk.configuration.payment_provider %>
    <li><strong>Payments.</strong> You enter your card on Stripe's page, and Stripe keeps it. We store your Stripe
      customer id, the two mandates that your assistant signs for each payment, the amount, the currency, Stripe's
      payment id, the receipt values and any refund. This demo uses Stripe's test mode: no real money moves.</li>
  <% end %>
  <% if Kiosk.configuration.kyc_provider %>
    <li><strong>Identity checks.</strong> We store only the facts that the KYC provider confirmed, for example
      <code>age_over_18</code>, and when it confirmed them. We never receive a document, a name or a date of
      birth.</li>
  <% end %>
</ul>
<h2>Server logs</h2>
<p>Each request writes a log line with its path, its parameters and the IP address it came from. We remove
  passwords, e-mail addresses, tokens and keys from the parameters before we write them. The server's system
  journal keeps these lines until it deletes its oldest lines to stay below its size limit.</p>
<p>We do not sell or share what we store. We set one cookie, the session cookie that keeps you signed in and
  protects our forms.</p>
